1
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:03,320
Why did you buy so many pineapple cakes?

2
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:03,680
To use as bait.

3
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:04,080
Guess.

4
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:06,960
What is it for?

5
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:11,280
What took you so long?

6
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:13,200
We got delayed by something.

7
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:14,400
How is it?

8
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:15,520
Did you spot him?

9
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:16,880
Not yet.

10
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:19,400
How do you know

11
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:21,130
Qian Yanqing will show up here?

12
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:23,410
Accurate intel from my informant.

13
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:26,200
Qian Yanqing bought a ticket to Dagu yesterday.

14
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:27,480
His hometown is Dagu.

15
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:29,680
That intersection.

16
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:31,480
It's the only way to the station.

17
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:35,039
Mr. Qian!

18
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:39,280
Don't run!

19
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:44,560
Screw you!

20
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:45,490
Pick it up later.

21
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:51,680
Flank him.

22
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:52,240
Go.

23
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,060
Don't come any closer!

24
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:00,840
Don't push me!

25
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:01,760
If you push me,

26
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,480
we'll die together!

27
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:04,800
Mr. Qian,

28
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,680
if you confess everything,

29
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:08,000
I'll plead for you

30
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,080
for leniency.

31
00:02:09,639 --> 00:02:10,699
Are you kidding me?

32
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:13,200
What I've done,

33
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:14,560
I know exactly.

34
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:16,280
I'll say it again.

35
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:17,880
Let me go,

36
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:18,640
or else

37
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:20,170
we'll die together!

38
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:21,200
Mr. Qian,

39
00:02:22,079 --> 00:02:24,280
you don't have to take the blame for everything.

40
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:26,280
What's the point of taking the fall alone?

41
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:28,010
What good does it do you, right?

42
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:29,400
Put down the grenade.

43
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:30,480
I'll help you.

44
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:31,880
Detective Jiang,

45
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:33,280
you have no idea

46
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:35,040
who you're up against,

47
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:36,800
what kind of big shot they are.

48
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:38,160
No matter who they are,

49
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:40,620
if they break the law, they will be arrested.

50
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:42,480
All of them.

51
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:44,680
Try and catch me.

52
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:46,440
Watch out.

53
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:50,320
Are you okay?

54
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:51,940
Don't move.

55
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:54,680
How is it?

56
00:02:59,040 --> 00:02:59,840
Keep running.

57
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:01,120
Keep running.

58
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:02,360
Keep running.

59
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:03,680
Keep running.

60
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:05,360
I told you not to run.

61
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:08,400
Why are you so strong?

62
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:09,680
Stand still.

63
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:10,600
Take him away.

64
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:13,440
Qian Yanqing.

65
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:15,800
As for your crimes and the Jingxiang Society,

66
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,880
we have already investigated them thoroughly.

67
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,880
I only have one question for you now.

68
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:21,000
Who is the Master?

69
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:22,840
I don't know who he is either.

70
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:24,840
Describe his physical appearance.

71
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:29,040
He is of medium build,

72
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,200
quite thin,

73
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:31,730
and has a loud voice.

74
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:32,600
Oh, right.

75
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:33,920
On his right arm,

76
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:36,060
he seems to have cigarette burns.

77
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:37,079
Three of them,

78
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:39,090
about the size of a fingernail.

79
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:42,320
Where exactly?

80
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:48,079
Here.

81
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:51,320
Jinwen,

82
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:53,560
how did you get these three scars?

83
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:56,480
I've asked you several times before, but you never told me.

84
00:03:56,480 --> 00:03:57,120
This?

85
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:58,840
I was naughty when I was a kid.

86
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:00,100
I got poked by a branch.

87
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:01,820
It's ancient history.

88
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,080
Hurry up and eat,

89
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:03,880
or it'll get cold.

90
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:04,880
Come on, eat more.

91
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:06,730
It doesn't look like a poke.

92
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:08,040
Master

93
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:10,930
gives a lecture on the 15th of every month.

94
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:12,440
He didn't come last month,

95
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:13,370
and up until now,

96
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:15,100
he hasn't shown up.

97
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:18,360
You guys interrogate him first.

98
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,959
I'm going out for a cup of tea.

99
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,880
Qian Yanqing, go on.

100
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:30,970
Is there anything else different?

101
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:32,780
What are you dawdling for?

102
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:43,159
Besides wearing a mask,

103
00:04:43,159 --> 00:04:45,080
is there anything else special?

104
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:48,340
He only appears on the 15th of every month

105
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:50,480
to preach at the base.

106
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:52,840
Preaches on the 15th of every month.

107
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:53,460
Jinwen.

108
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,640
Do you want to spend the Mid-Autumn Festival at my house?

109
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:58,080
No, I have a mission.

110
00:04:59,080 --> 00:04:59,840
Wait.

111
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:03,000
I noticed that not only on the Mid-Autumn Festival,

112
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,880
but you also go out on missions on the 15th of every month.

113
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:08,140
Why? Are you going to turn into a monster?

114
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:09,800
Even if I turn into a monster,

115
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:11,480
I'll snatch you away first.

116
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:18,680
Siyao.

117
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:22,880
What are you looking at?

118
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:23,680
Who let you in?

119
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,240
Why didn't you knock?

120
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:27,730
I've been knocking for a long time.

121
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:30,000
What's wrong?

122
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:32,000
I need to know

123
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:34,440
Lin Jinwen's recent attendance records.

124
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:35,500
Go find them for me.

125
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:38,340
Why are you suddenly looking at this?

126
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:40,060
Don't ask what you shouldn't.

127
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:40,840
Okay.

128
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:41,810
Don't forget

129
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:44,440
to take the things I bought for you back with you.

130
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:45,170
What things?

131
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:47,170
I bought you so much.

132
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:50,000
You mean

133
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:52,100
those pineapple cakes

134
00:05:52,640 --> 00:05:53,300
were for me?

135
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:57,080
What's this for?

136
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:59,080
Ningning told me everything.

137
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:00,560
It was you who insisted on rushing to

138
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:02,480
the Jingxiang Society's headquarters to save me.

139
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:03,280
Alright.

140
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:08,880
For you.

141
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:26,600
Hey you,

142
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:28,560
where is Detective Jiang?

143
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:30,280
Who are you calling 'hey you'?

144
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:32,040
Miss Huo,

145
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:33,500
where is Detective Jiang?

146
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:34,540
He didn't come.

147
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:36,700
He didn't come.

148
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:38,520
What?

149
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:39,880
Does our Detective Jiang need to

150
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:41,240
ask you for leave?

151
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:43,680
That won't be necessary.

152
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:45,760
Detective Jiang has been working too hard lately.

153
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:47,220
He needs a good day of rest.

154
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:49,480
Even draft animals need a good rest.

155
00:06:49,880 --> 00:06:50,880
That makes sense.

156
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:52,760
Looks like we don't need to investigate today.

157
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:53,760
Stop right there.

158
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:55,560
Am I invisible?

159
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:57,240
Let me tell you.

160
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,280
As long as I'm here,

161
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:00,940
there's no case I can't solve.

162
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:04,410
Where are you going?

163
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:08,800
It's noon.

164
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:09,880
I'm hungry.

165
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:12,610
You're buying me lunch.

166
00:07:13,280 --> 00:07:14,960
I'll treat you.

167
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:24,810
Who treats a girl to just steamed buns?

168
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:25,760
Boss,

169
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,560
give him two more baskets of steamed buns.

170
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:28,690
Let him eat to death.

171
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:31,880
Thank you.

172
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:32,880
You're welcome.

173
00:07:32,880 --> 00:07:33,560
Eat.

174
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:36,520
Stop messing around.

175
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:37,320
Let me ask you,

176
00:07:38,760 --> 00:07:40,240
don't you think Detective Jiang

177
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,600
was a bit unusual yesterday?

178
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:43,240
How dare you talk about my senior sister?

179
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:44,640
I'm talking about serious business.

180
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:45,480
Spit it out.

181
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:47,600
Yesterday,

182
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:50,080
when Qian Yanqing mentioned the Master,

183
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:51,409
she looked distracted,

184
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:52,680
and then went out.

185
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:54,640
So what?

186
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,600
Are you going to keep farting

187
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:57,640
one by one?

188
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:00,040
What I mean is,

189
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:02,160
no, I mean what if

190
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:03,760
Detective Jiang

191
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:04,840
and the Master

192
00:08:04,960 --> 00:08:06,600
actually knew each other a long time ago,

193
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:08,660
and they have a secret relationship?

194
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:10,800
A mouse eating arsenic.

195
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:12,600
I think you have a death wish.

196
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:13,320
Okay.

197
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:15,840
Then what's your brilliant idea, Officer Huo?

198
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:18,280
Then let me give you some pointers.

199
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:19,290
What's this?

200
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:21,560
Qian Yanqing said

201
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:22,960
this was given by the Master

202
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:25,080
to the senior members of the Jingxiang Society.

203
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:26,480
Look at the pattern on it.

204
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:27,920
Can you see anything?

205
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:30,120
No.

206
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:31,600
Seed embroidery.

207
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:35,809
I've seen this since I was a kid.

208
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:37,440
Normal seed embroidery

209
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:39,320
uses double threads

210
00:08:39,559 --> 00:08:41,490
wrapped around once to make a seed.

211
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:44,159
This one uses a single thread

212
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:46,480
wrapped around twice to make a seed.

213
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:49,300
And the embroidery thread shines with gold.

214
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:50,440
This uses...

215
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:52,560
Really?

216
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:54,480
Go on.

217
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:57,640
There is only one place in the whole city

218
00:08:57,800 --> 00:09:00,080
that uses this embroidery method and thread to make sachets.

219
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:01,640
Furui Embroidery Shop.

220
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:05,280
Boss.

221
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:05,960
You two,

222
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:07,120
what do you need?

223
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:07,640
Boss,

224
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:09,080
take a look.

225
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:10,720
Was this sachet

226
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:12,080
custom-made here?

227
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:18,560
Xiao Lin did it.

228
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:19,880
Who ordered it?

229
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:21,880
Who?

230
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:24,210
I have some impression.

231
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:24,760
But,

232
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:26,360
I don't know his name.

233
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:28,640
What did he look like?

234
00:09:28,760 --> 00:09:30,020
Do you still remember?

235
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:32,600
About average height.

236
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:33,720
Right.

237
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,160
I remember.

238
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:37,640
Although he was wearing a long gown,

239
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:39,880
the leather shoes he wore

240
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:42,280
were the kind only police officers can wear,

241
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:44,080
standard Meihua leather shoes.

242
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:50,040
This is the chief of Linjia Village.

243
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:51,640
Greetings, Officer.

244
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:52,960
If you need anything from me,

245
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:54,600
I will tell you everything I know.

246
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:55,960
Don't be nervous, Chief.

247
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:57,600
I just want to ask you about someone.

248
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:58,880
His name is Lin Jinwen,

249
00:09:58,880 --> 00:10:00,080
from Linjia Village.

250
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:01,560
Lin Jinwen?

251
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:03,680
Everyone in our village is surnamed Lin.

252
00:10:03,680 --> 00:10:05,160
I really don't remember this name.

253
00:10:05,160 --> 00:10:06,690
He is 28 years old this year.

254
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:08,560
He left to become a soldier a long time ago.

255
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:09,960
Officer, it's like this.

256
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,080
Those warlords

257
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:13,960
come to our village every now and then to conscript men.

258
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:16,040
Many people from our village became soldiers.

259
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:17,970
I really don't remember this name.

260
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,160
Thank you, Chief.

261
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:20,490
You're welcome.

262
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:31,200
It seems I still know too little about him.

263
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:33,280
I only know he is from Linjia Village.

264
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:34,280
Don't lose heart.

265
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:36,220
Isn't there another clue?

266
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:37,360
You mean...

267
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:38,680
The army.

268
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:41,880
I've already sent someone to contact Commander Liu.

269
00:10:41,880 --> 00:10:43,140
He should be here soon.

270
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:46,130
Commander Liu has arrived!

271
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:49,040
Commander Liu,

272
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:50,100
please have a seat.

273
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:52,800
Hello, Commander Liu.

274
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:53,840
I am Jiang Siyao.

275
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:55,680
You have quite a reputation.

276
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:58,240
Not as famous as Commander Liu.

277
00:10:58,400 --> 00:10:58,880
Speak.

278
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,530
What do you want from me?

279
00:11:01,520 --> 00:11:03,250
I want to ask you about someone.

280
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:04,480
Ten years ago,

281
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:05,640
you had a soldier under your command

282
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:06,960
named Lin Jinwen.

283
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:09,120
Lin Jinwen.

284
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:12,760
He used to be a squad leader under my command.

285
00:11:12,760 --> 00:11:13,560
Ten years ago,

286
00:11:13,880 --> 00:11:15,480
when we were fighting the Queue Army.

287
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:16,480
He died in battle.

288
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:18,280
He died in battle.

289
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:18,880
Yes.

290
00:11:19,360 --> 00:11:20,690
His parents died early.

291
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:23,160
He had been with me since he was a teenager.

292
00:11:23,160 --> 00:11:24,240
I originally planned

293
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:26,900
for him to transfer to be a police officer later.

294
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:27,880
What a pity.

295
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:30,620
Commander Liu,

296
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:32,400
is this the person?

297
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:37,620
This person is not Lin Jinwen.

298
00:11:39,160 --> 00:11:39,890
Let me think.

299
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:41,760
His name is

300
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,000
Lin Yousheng.

301
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:46,480
Lin Yousheng.

302
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:47,520
Right.

303
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:50,040
I was still a company commander back then.

304
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:51,640
He came to me to join the army.

305
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:54,010
I didn't want him because he was too young.

306
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:56,560
But seeing he was homeless,

307
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:57,760
I took pity on him

308
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:59,740
and let him follow Lin Jinwen.

309
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:01,800
But after Lin Jinwen died in battle,

310
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:03,680
no one knows where he went.

311
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:06,280
Lin Yousheng.

312
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:09,480
His name is actually Lin Yousheng.
